title: Black Box
text: White goes in and white comes out, as if the box weren't there. But something inside it has to show blue, and something has to show red. Take the light apart if you must; just put it back.
trick: a prism breaks the white beam inside the box; twisters only turn left, and exactly that brings the fan back together: green takes one twister and red two to converge on a second prism, which merges all three into white on the original line
motif: pictogram (a sealed box with an input and an output pipe)
expect: merges>=1, recolours>=1
---
L 0 4 2 w
*P 4 4 0 k
*W 7 7 0 k
*W 4 10 0 k
*W 10 10 0 k
*P 10 4 1 k
T 13 4 0 ?
T 7 4 0 ?
T 10 7 0 ?
% walls: the box and its two pipes
